WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.909
<i>Long ago. a mythic
battle between good and evil</i>

3
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.673
<i>played out in ancient China.</i>

4
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.194
<i>The country was torn by civil war.</i>

5
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.352
<i>with many kingdoms
struggling for land and power.</i>

6
00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:53.431
<i>But one king had a ruthless ambition
to make himself emperor by the sword.</i>

7
00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.188
Leave me.

8
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.316
Prepare for war!

9
00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:24.192
<i>The other rulers hired assassins
to kill the King</i>

10
00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.794
<i>before he could conquer them all.</i>

11
00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.272
Stop! I am not harmed.

12
00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:14.869
We attack tonight!

13
00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:32.431
<i>Kingdom by kingdom.
his army swept away everything in its path.</i>

14
00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.195
<i>and anyone who resisted met a terrible fate.</i>

15
00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:40.918
<i>The country was his.</i>

16
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.037
<i>He was now Emperor of All Under Heaven.</i>

17
00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:50.191
<i>He enslaved his conquered enemies
and forced them to build his Great Wall.</i>

18
00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.034
<i>When they were dead or useless.
he had them buried beneath it.</i>

19
00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:28.119
<i>The Emperor's mystics taught him
mastery over the five elements.</i>

20
00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.988
<i>fire. water. earth. wood and metal.</i>

21
00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.310
<i>His power seemed without limit.</i>

22
00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.476
<i>He was master of millions.</i>

23
00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:45.189
<i>but like the lowliest peasant.
he could not stop growing old.</i>

24
00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:50.273
I have too much to do for one lifetime.

25
00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:54.274
<i>He needed to defeat
his last enemy. death itself.</i>

26
00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.432
<i>One day. news came of a powerful witch</i>

27
00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:07.910
<i>who was rumoured to know
the secret to eternal life.</i>

28
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:13.028
<i>He ordered General Ming. his oldest friend
and trusted ally. to find her.</i>

29
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.150
<i>The witch was named Zi Yuan.</i>

30
00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.277
<i>and she was nothing
like the General expected.</i>

31
00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:39.514
Your Majesty...

32
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:45.989
Rise up.

33
00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:52.556
I do not possess the secret of
immortality. my Lord...

34
00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.473
...but I know where to find it.

35
00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:57.869
General...

36
00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.038
No man is to touch her.

37
00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:05.750
She is mine.

38
00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:14.229
<i>On the western border
stood the Monastery of Turfan.</i>

39
00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:18.154
<i>There was housed the greatest library
in the ancient world.</i>

40
00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:22.279
<i>and Zi Yuan was sure
the secret to eternal life was here.</i>

41
00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.031
This is a key.

42
00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:58.399
<i>It was the long lost
oracle bones.</i>

43
00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:02.632
<i>a collection of all the mystical secrets
of the ancient world.</i>

44
00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:08.033
<i>The Emperor's answer was here
along with other magic beyond imagining.</i>

45
00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:20.597
You have served me well.

46
00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:26.192
I will grant you anything you desire.

47
00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:31.115
I want to spend my life with General Ming.

48
00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:34.793
Of course.

49
00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:36.349
Read.

50
00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:55.390
<i>She cast the spell in Sanskrit.</i>

51
00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:59.359
<i>an ancient language
that the Emperor did not understand.</i>

52
00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:07.189
I feel your spell working.

53
00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:14.158
I am now immortal.

54
00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:18.233
Come. I want to show you something.

55
00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:36.755
Become my queen and I will let him live.

56
00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:40.795
Do what he says! Save yourself!

57
00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:46.835
You will never keep your word.

58
00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:49.389
You are right.

59
00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.751
Now. join General Ming in hell.

60
00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:22.034
What did you do to me?

61
00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:25.036
I cursed you and your army.

62
00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.519
Surround the Palace!

63
00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:41.993
The Emperor is in trouble!

64
00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:00.190
<i>The curse must never be lifted.</i>

65
00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:04.592
<i>or the Emperor will rise again
to enslave all of mankind.</i>

66
00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:09.310
<i>On that dark day.
there will be nothing and no one to save us.</i>

67
00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:26.118
You can run. but you can't hide.

68
00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:33.629
One o'clock.

69
00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:35.358
OXFORDSHIRE. ENGLAND

70
00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:40.910
Ten o'clock. one o'clock. Ten o'clock. one...

71
00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.798
And this is something for grown men to do?

72
00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:53.914
Come on.

73
00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:03.833
Bite on this.

74
00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.756
Evy. I'm home!

75
00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:25.752
Mrs O'Connell is at her book reading. sir.
She'll be home for dinner.

76
00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:29.435
Oh. right. Well. that's great.
'cause we're having fish.

77
00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:34.238
You didn't think I'd catch anything.
did you?

78
00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.754
I had the utmost confidence. sir.

79
00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:43.356
There's a hook in your neck. sir.
Shall I fetch the wire cutters?

80
00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:52.989
<i>Fall back! Follow me!
Move! Move! Move! Move!</i>

81
00:10:57.360 --> 00:10:59.635
<i>"Now safely aboard the airship
with the mummy finally vanquished.</i>

82
00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:00.755
LONDON

83
00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:04.149
<i>"Dash swept Scarlet into his arms.</i>

84
00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:09.315
"'Oh. God. Scarlet. I thought I'd lost you.'
'For a moment there. you did.'

85
00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:12.474
"Bathed in rays of golden sunlight.

86
00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:17.429
"our heroes sealed their reunion
with a kiss of timeless passion.

87
00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:20.910
"their love deeper and truer than ever."

88
00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:29.515
Mrs O'Connell. we're all dying to know.

89
00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:32.956
is the Scarlet O'Keefe character
really based on you?

90
00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:37.677
Honestly. I can say
she's a completely different person.

91
00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.671
- Any more questions?
-  Mrs O'Connell...

92
00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:44.117
Mrs O'Connell. is your life today
as exciting as it was before the war?

93
00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:47.836
I wish my life were that exciting now.

94
00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:49.273
Will there be another book
in the series?

95
00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:51.828
Do you believe in happy endings?

96
00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:56.791
Isn't this blissful?

97
00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:00.632
Dinner at home.

98
00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:04.196
- Every night.
- Every night.

99
00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:08.629
- Here's to retirement.
- May we stay this happy forever.

100
00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:25.514
Still no letter from Alex.
I've sent him three in the last month.

101
00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:26.715
Yeah. well. what do you expect?

102
00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:27.869
The only time we ever hear from that kid

103
00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:30.076
is when he's getting kicked out of college
or he needs more money.

104
00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:33.072
I'm sure he's just buried in his studies.

105
00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:43.199
- So. how did your book reading go?
- Oh. fine. Thank you.

106
00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:46.918
Until they asked me. "When will there
be another Mummy adventure?"

107
00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.434
Yeah. but you did promise the publisher
a third book.

108
00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:50.555
I know.

109
00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:54.792
But I spend my nights staring
at a blank page. completely blocked.

110
00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:59.829
We could skip dinner. and I could

111
00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:04.994
attempt to inspire you upstairs.

112
00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:08.751
Oh. that's so sweet of you. darling.

113
00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:13.277
But I'm going to sit at that typewriter
until something exciting comes out.

114
00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:16.832
Thank you.

115
00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:21.438
Trout. How lovely!

116
00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:28.635
I'm so happy you found a hobby
that doesn't involve guns.

117
00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:38.717
NINGXIA PROVINCE. CHINA

118
00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:51.399
Don't worry. we'll find the entrance today.

119
00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:55.313
Li Tung. what's for lunch?

120
00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:56.389
Noodle soup.

121
00:13:56.800 --> 00:13:58.153
Very good.

122
00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:05.996
Good. Wilson's back.

123
00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:09.510
You're a couple days late. Professor.

124
00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:11.033
I was beginning to think
you'd run into bandits.

125
00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:13.031
Oh. my dear fellow.
thank you for the concern.

126
00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:14.758
- Are you thirsty?
- Oh. yes. please.

127
00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.796
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

128
00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.876
You know.
when I saw you standing up there.

129
00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:22.030
I thought I was looking at your father.

130
00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:23.792
You really are Rick O'Connell's son.

131
00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:28.510
Yeah. well. hopefully after today.
he'll be known as Alex O'Connell's father.

132
00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:31.194
What a powerful face!

133
00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:35.068
When I told my colleagues at the museum
that you had discovered the Colossus.

134
00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:36.675
they were thrilled.

135
00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:38.876
- Yes. however...
- I know.

136
00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:40.951
When am I gonna get in that tomb?

137
00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:42.996
Don't let the buggers get you down.

138
00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:45.389
It was you that discovered
the Bembridge journal.

139
00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:47.869
and with it. you'll discover the Emperor.

140
00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:51.555
- I have complete faith in you. Alex.
- Thank you. Professor.

141
00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.872
Thanks for believing in me.

142
00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.912
We found it! We found the door!

143
00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:02.792
<i>Bad Mummy.</i>

144
00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:05.599
Yeah.

145
00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:08.911
<i>Vile Mummy?</i>

146
00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:12.514
<i>No. Cursed Mummy!</i>

147
00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:15.394
<i>Mysterious Mummy.</i>

148
00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:19.590
<i>Malignant Mummy.</i>

149
00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:25.791
Prepare to die!

150
00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:28.873
Take that!

151
00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:38.188
Rick!

152
00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.837
Darling. where are you?

153
00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:54.190
I'm ready to be inspired.

154
00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:04.514
Do you remember the time
the mummy had me tied down?

155
00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:08.388
And you came to save me and you cut...

156
00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:12.553
No! You tore open the ropes
is what you did.

157
00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:15.359
just as he was about to plunge his...

158
00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:19.239
Oh. rats.

159
00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:47.199
Watch out!

160
00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.269
- Emperor didn't want any houseguests.
- Yeah.

161
00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:58.469
Stay together.

162
00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:24.717
Sir Colin Bembridge.

163
00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:26.879
Oh. gee...

164
00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:29.955
He went searching for this tomb
70 years ago.

165
00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:31.917
They left him like this as a warning.

166
00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.673
Unfortunately. this is not the dead man
that's gonna make us famous.

167
00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:36.432
Let's keep moving.

168
00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:13.073
Look at it. Alex.

169
00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:15.593
Look at it!

170
00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:54.159
Chu Wah!

171
00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:37.512
- Chu Wah.
- No. no. don't. don't. don't.

172
00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:40.194
Alex. Alex. they're dead! Come on.

173
00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:43.272
This kind of danger goes with the territory.
You know that better than anyone.

174
00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:44.588
Alex!

175
00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:50.233
- Yes?
- Okay.

176
00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:51.673
- Yes?
- Yeah.

177
00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:56.677
All right. good chap. Okay. Good chap.
Oh. Jesus.

178
00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:04.916
All the warriors are facing in to this point.

179
00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:08.197
- as if awaiting an order from the Emperor.
- Well. then. where is he?

180
00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:12.671
Listen. you don't think some bloody grave
robber's beaten us to the prize. do you?

181
00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:14.398
No. he's still here.

182
00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:17.552
You see. this is a feng shui compass.

183
00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:27.874
Okay. Now. This...

184
00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:29.791
Okay. this is true north.

185
00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:33.953
but the feng shui compass
is set in the opposite direction.

186
00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:36.031
- All right. we need to realign it.
- All right.

187
00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:38.111
- All right. here we go.
- All right.

188
00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:02.076
Alex! Alex. speak to me!

189
00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:04.232
Are you all right?

190
00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:07.749
- Alex!
- I'm fine.

191
00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:11.308
Tell me. have we found the Emperor?

192
00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:16.194
Alex!

193
00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:24.874
What is it?

194
00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:27.793
It's only the greatest find since King Tut!

195
00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:35.274
"If he is awakened.
all mortals should despair."

196
00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:37.237
It's definitely him!

197
00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:43.715
Even had his concubines buried alive
with him.

198
00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:45.119
Selfish bastard.

199
00:21:45.720 --> 00:21:48.712
Hey. Professor Wilson.
you want to come down and take a look?

200
00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:51.837
Or are you so overwhelmed you can't talk?

201
00:22:14.800 --> 00:22:16.119
Wilson!

202
00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:27.317
Let's go. Professor.
We've got a lot of work to do.

203
00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:28.276
All right.

204
00:23:34.200 --> 00:23:35.758
First of all. I'd just like to say

205
00:23:35.840 --> 00:23:38.957
that the Foreign Office appreciates
all that you did during the war.

206
00:23:39.040 --> 00:23:43.192
But I've been sent to offer you
one last assignment.

207
00:23:43.880 --> 00:23:48.078
I'm afraid we've retired
from the espionage game. haven't we. dear?

208
00:23:48.160 --> 00:23:50.230
Yeah. we've... We don't do that any more.
We're finished.

209
00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:52.550
- Not at all.
- Completely done.

210
00:23:54.480 --> 00:23:57.597
But just out of curiosity.
what is the mission anyway?

211
00:23:57.680 --> 00:24:00.877
We need you to courier this to Shanghai.

212
00:24:04.200 --> 00:24:07.431
- Nice piece of ice.
- It's the Eye of Shangri-La.

213
00:24:07.520 --> 00:24:10.876
If you believe the legend.
it points the way to the Pool of Eternal Life.

214
00:24:10.960 --> 00:24:13.030
It was smuggled out of China in 1940.

215
00:24:13.120 --> 00:24:15.759
Now. the government would like
to return it to the Shanghai Museum

216
00:24:15.840 --> 00:24:19.116
as a sign of good faith
to the Chinese people.

217
00:24:19.200 --> 00:24:22.954
And with your expertise in the field.
we naturally thought of you.

218
00:24:23.040 --> 00:24:25.838
Oh. we'd be so flattered.

219
00:24:27.840 --> 00:24:31.515
But Rick and I. we made a promise
to each other after the war

220
00:24:31.600 --> 00:24:34.558
that we would settle down.

221
00:24:34.640 --> 00:24:37.359
- That's right. yeah. we did. didn't we? We...
- I see.

222
00:24:37.440 --> 00:24:40.238
Well. I must admit I am a little disappointed.

223
00:24:40.320 --> 00:24:43.596
Postwar China is very dangerous.

224
00:24:43.680 --> 00:24:48.390
There are a lot of factions that would love
to get their hands on the Eye of Shangri-La.

225
00:24:48.480 --> 00:24:51.950
In lesser hands.
the Eye could be lost forever.

226
00:24:52.720 --> 00:24:54.312
We couldn't let that happen. could we?

227
00:24:54.400 --> 00:24:56.709
No. that could be bad for the world.

228
00:24:56.800 --> 00:24:58.870
- The world... Terrible.
- Yeah.

229
00:24:59.920 --> 00:25:01.433
You know. she has a brother
who lives in Shanghai.

230
00:25:01.520 --> 00:25:03.272
- Jonathan!
- Yes.

231
00:25:03.360 --> 00:25:05.157
He owns a nightclub. if I'm not mistaken.

232
00:25:05.240 --> 00:25:06.639
We have been meaning to visit. We could...

233
00:25:06.720 --> 00:25:07.948
- We should...
...drop in and surprise him.

234
00:25:08.040 --> 00:25:09.632
- Say hello.
- Why not?

235
00:25:09.720 --> 00:25:12.871
Does this mean
we can count on you one last time?

236
00:25:14.160 --> 00:25:15.149
Yes.

237
00:25:18.680 --> 00:25:20.352
SHANGHAI. CHINA

238
00:25:20.440 --> 00:25:22.317
CHINESE NEW YEAR. 1947

239
00:25:48.080 --> 00:25:49.229
There we are.

240
00:25:50.840 --> 00:25:52.876
Here's to you. Princess.

241
00:25:52.960 --> 00:25:56.077
And Imhotep.
May the bugger actually stay dead.

242
00:25:57.280 --> 00:25:58.633
Ding-dong.

243
00:26:06.440 --> 00:26:08.795
Hi. can you buy a drink for me?

244
00:26:09.640 --> 00:26:12.438
Excuse me. Alex! Alex! You're back again.

245
00:26:12.520 --> 00:26:13.919
Come here. Alex. Let me get you a drink.

246
00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:16.389
Smooth special for the pup. huh?
The explorer.

247
00:26:18.480 --> 00:26:19.799
Make that two.

248
00:26:19.880 --> 00:26:22.314
Sorry. Uncle Jon. but I got a better offer.

249
00:26:22.400 --> 00:26:25.949
No. no. Alex. No. look.
Listen. how can I... Come here.

250
00:26:26.040 --> 00:26:27.758
To put it in archaeological terms.

251
00:26:27.840 --> 00:26:29.956
that's a tomb
in which many pharaohs have lain.

252
00:26:30.040 --> 00:26:32.838
Now. listen. listen.
just think about me for a moment. all right?

253
00:26:32.920 --> 00:26:36.549
Your discovery will go public in a few days.
and your parents are sure to find out.

254
00:26:36.640 --> 00:26:39.074
They're not gonna be happy
you've dropped out of school. And...

255
00:26:39.160 --> 00:26:42.835
Will you relax. Uncle Jon? Okay? I'm here.
They're a long way away.

256
00:26:42.920 --> 00:26:45.639
- Alex...
- Excuse me. okay?

257
00:26:45.720 --> 00:26:47.915
I have some excavation to do.

258
00:26:55.720 --> 00:26:57.039
Jonathan!

259
00:27:01.120 --> 00:27:04.157
You're in China! Evy. Rick.

260
00:27:04.240 --> 00:27:06.515
What are you... It's so...
I didn't even...

261
00:27:06.600 --> 00:27:09.672
Brother. how lovely to see you.

262
00:27:09.760 --> 00:27:11.432
I had no idea he was here!

263
00:27:11.520 --> 00:27:12.919
- Who was here?
- Who?

264
00:27:14.800 --> 00:27:16.791
This happens every time!

265
00:27:17.680 --> 00:27:19.750
Every man in the bar!

266
00:27:19.840 --> 00:27:20.875
- Dad?
- Alex!

267
00:27:20.960 --> 00:27:22.552
I don't know what to do with you!
- He's just a boy!

268
00:27:22.640 --> 00:27:25.837
- I can't leave the room for 10 minutes!
- I didn't... Go away! Go to hell!

269
00:27:25.920 --> 00:27:27.876
- I'm sick of it!
- Let's go get lover-boy!

270
00:27:27.960 --> 00:27:29.837
I'm gonna kill you. kid!

271
00:27:29.920 --> 00:27:32.070
Not so fast. that's my kid.

272
00:27:34.080 --> 00:27:37.197
- Mad Dog Maguire?
- Ricochet O'Connell.

273
00:27:37.680 --> 00:27:40.069
- Hey. hey.
- What are you doing here?

274
00:27:40.160 --> 00:27:42.913
- Alex! Sweetheart! Are you all right?
- Just a little family get-together. folks.

275
00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:46.276
Come on.
let's get back to having a good time. Music!

276
00:27:46.760 --> 00:27:47.749
How long has it been?

277
00:27:47.840 --> 00:27:50.559
Egypt. '23. French Foreign Legion.

278
00:27:51.880 --> 00:27:53.757
This guy could land a plane
on anything. you...

279
00:27:53.840 --> 00:27:56.354
- Why are you here?
- Ricochet. he had his hands all over me girl.

280
00:27:56.440 --> 00:27:58.635
Now. son or no son.
I gotta give him a beating!

281
00:27:58.720 --> 00:28:00.950
- Get out of the way. Dad.
- Sit down.

282
00:28:01.040 --> 00:28:03.679
Now as much as I'd really like you
to teach him a valuable lesson...

283
00:28:03.760 --> 00:28:05.352
His mother would be upset! Very upset.

284
00:28:05.440 --> 00:28:06.919
You have a lot of explaining to do.
young man.

285
00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:08.149
I got a wife now. and a kid.

286
00:28:08.240 --> 00:28:10.310
Things are a little bit different.
I'm sure you understand.

287
00:28:10.400 --> 00:28:12.038
- Yeah.
- Let me make it up to you.

288
00:28:13.280 --> 00:28:15.316
We're just surprised to see you here.
That's all.

289
00:28:15.400 --> 00:28:16.753
Who's gonna pay
for all this damage?

290
00:28:16.840 --> 00:28:18.068
All right?

291
00:28:18.160 --> 00:28:19.149
I'm not here five minutes.

292
00:28:19.240 --> 00:28:21.037
and I'm already pulling your fanny
out of the fire.

293
00:28:21.120 --> 00:28:22.109
You're going back to college.

294
00:28:22.200 --> 00:28:25.237
How'd you think this was gonna work. Dad?
You two show up. tell me what to do?

295
00:28:25.320 --> 00:28:29.598
No. But we should sit down
and discuss this like a family.

296
00:28:29.680 --> 00:28:32.353
No offence. Mom.
but we haven't been a family in a long time.

297
00:28:32.440 --> 00:28:34.396
Hey. don't you turn your back on me. Alex!

298
00:28:34.480 --> 00:28:36.710
Alex. just... Alex. come here.

299
00:28:38.640 --> 00:28:40.073
Can you...

300
00:28:41.320 --> 00:28:43.436
Don't look at me like that.

301
00:28:49.080 --> 00:28:51.355
- It's all your fault!
- My fault?

302
00:28:51.440 --> 00:28:53.078
You're the one
that's always smothering him.

303
00:28:53.160 --> 00:28:55.594
You couldn't leave him alone
for five minutes without wiping his nose.

304
00:28:55.680 --> 00:28:59.275
Perhaps I was overcompensating for the fact
that you never took an interest in his life.

305
00:28:59.360 --> 00:29:01.920
His life was my top priority.

306
00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:04.468
How many times did I save that kid
from breaking his neck?

307
00:29:04.560 --> 00:29:06.710
A little warmth and encouragement
would have been nice.

308
00:29:06.800 --> 00:29:09.394
I'm his father. It's implied.

309
00:29:12.440 --> 00:29:16.115
We've spent our entire lives
searching for priceless artefacts.

310
00:29:16.200 --> 00:29:17.713
and the one thing
that's most precious to us.

311
00:29:17.800 --> 00:29:18.789
we've lost.

312
00:29:20.440 --> 00:29:25.230
We can't let Alex become some stranger
in pictures on our mantle.

313
00:29:25.960 --> 00:29:27.632
- We can't let that happen.
- No. we can't.

314
00:29:27.720 --> 00:29:29.756
How are we gonna fix this?

315
00:29:31.280 --> 00:29:33.396
We need to do it together.

316
00:29:39.640 --> 00:29:43.838
PARAMILITARY OUTPOST
WESTERN CHINA

317
00:30:07.400 --> 00:30:10.073
The O'Connells are in Shanghai.

318
00:30:10.640 --> 00:30:13.029
Do they have the Eye of Shangri-La?

319
00:30:13.120 --> 00:30:15.395
Our spy says they do.

320
00:30:15.880 --> 00:30:16.869
Good.

321
00:30:17.080 --> 00:30:18.195
Assemble the troops!

322
00:30:18.280 --> 00:30:19.269
Yes sir.

323
00:30:23.600 --> 00:30:24.589
Soldiers!

324
00:30:25.160 --> 00:30:28.436
Soon all our training and sacrifice...

325
00:30:29.080 --> 00:30:31.514
will bear great fruit.

326
00:30:32.520 --> 00:30:35.637
It is my dream to raise our Emperor
from his tomb.

327
00:30:36.320 --> 00:30:39.312
Only He can bring order out of this chaos.

328
00:30:40.320 --> 00:30:41.309
Soldiers...

329
00:30:42.480 --> 00:30:46.029
tonight our great battle begins!

330
00:30:56.760 --> 00:31:00.116
You know. this might have been faster
if we took a rickshaw.

331
00:31:00.200 --> 00:31:02.430
It's Chinese New Year.

332
00:31:02.520 --> 00:31:03.509
Don't you just love this country?

333
00:31:03.600 --> 00:31:06.831
They have so many extra little holidays.
and drinking is mandatory.

334
00:31:06.920 --> 00:31:09.388
I can't believe
we get to see your first big discovery.

335
00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:10.469
It's so exciting.

336
00:31:10.560 --> 00:31:12.949
Well. after last night.
I'm surprised you want to see it at all.

337
00:31:14.360 --> 00:31:16.874
Listen.
I'll pick you up in about an hour.

338
00:31:16.960 --> 00:31:18.188
You're not coming?

339
00:31:18.280 --> 00:31:21.477
No. no.
I've seen enough mummies to last a lifetime.

340
00:31:32.320 --> 00:31:33.719
There he is.

341
00:31:34.320 --> 00:31:37.596
Oh. my darling. very impressive.

342
00:31:38.520 --> 00:31:40.158
When do you get to open the sarcophagus?

343
00:31:40.240 --> 00:31:42.196
Well.
after the official red tape has been cut.

344
00:31:42.280 --> 00:31:45.431
Do the words "rest in peace"
mean anything to you two?

345
00:31:45.520 --> 00:31:49.069
So. Mom. why don't you stick around
for the next few days.

346
00:31:49.160 --> 00:31:50.354
and we can open it together?

347
00:31:50.440 --> 00:31:51.793
I would like that very much. thanks.

348
00:31:51.880 --> 00:31:54.075
Alex. why don't you go
and tell Professor Wilson

349
00:31:54.160 --> 00:31:56.151
that we're here. You know...

350
00:31:56.240 --> 00:31:57.559
No problem. Great.

351
00:31:57.640 --> 00:32:00.677
Just don't wake the big guy up
while I'm gone.

352
00:32:07.160 --> 00:32:08.559
Hey. Alex.

353
00:32:09.160 --> 00:32:13.631
You know. this is all really. really big stuff.

354
00:32:16.920 --> 00:32:18.831
Whatever you say. Dad.

355
00:32:54.400 --> 00:32:55.594
What?

356
00:32:56.560 --> 00:33:01.395
You just have a certain glow about you
this evening I haven't seen in a long time.

357
00:33:02.840 --> 00:33:05.638
I guess mummies bring out the best in me.

358
00:33:06.800 --> 00:33:10.190
Take a wrong turn at Cairo?
Sorry to interrupt.

359
00:33:11.760 --> 00:33:13.637
- Roger.
- Professor Roger Wilson.

360
00:33:13.720 --> 00:33:14.994
Rick.

361
00:33:15.080 --> 00:33:18.470
You know. when Alex told me
that you had gone legit.

362
00:33:18.560 --> 00:33:20.516
I just couldn't believe my ears.

363
00:33:20.600 --> 00:33:24.149
Well. now I just pillage tombs
in the name of preservation. Evelyn.

364
00:33:24.240 --> 00:33:28.199
- Congratulations on your latest discovery.
- Alex deserves all the credit.

365
00:33:28.280 --> 00:33:30.271
He's one hell of a kid.
He's like the son I never had.

366
00:33:30.360 --> 00:33:31.634
And he's the only one we've got.

367
00:33:31.720 --> 00:33:33.676
so the next time you send him
on one of your field trips.

368
00:33:33.760 --> 00:33:34.988
you give us the heads-up first.

369
00:33:35.080 --> 00:33:37.355
Yes. yes. of course.

370
00:33:37.440 --> 00:33:40.716
And now. I believe you have
something that belongs to us.

371
00:33:40.800 --> 00:33:42.313
What's that?

372
00:33:42.400 --> 00:33:43.958
Oh. you mean this?

373
00:33:47.480 --> 00:33:48.913
I'm sorry...

374
00:33:50.480 --> 00:33:52.232
There. go ahead.

375
00:33:52.320 --> 00:33:54.038
All yours. Rog.

376
00:33:54.960 --> 00:33:57.428
I knew I could rely on you two.

377
00:33:59.000 --> 00:34:02.913
I'm afraid your work is not done yet.
Mr and Mrs O'Connell.

378
00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:06.754
I'd like to introduce you to a friend of mine.
General Yang.

379
00:34:06.840 --> 00:34:07.989
Roger!

380
00:34:08.440 --> 00:34:12.592
Well. he is the man who financed Alex's dig.
We're in this together.

381
00:34:13.440 --> 00:34:15.351
Cheek by jowl. General.

382
00:34:17.280 --> 00:34:18.713
Search him.

383
00:34:20.560 --> 00:34:24.519
No. The Eye belongs to the Chinese people.
You can't do this.

384
00:34:24.600 --> 00:34:28.912
So. Rog. you snake. how much did...

385
00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:31.673
Is it Yin and Yang? ...pay you?

386
00:34:31.760 --> 00:34:34.194
Enough to pull strings at the Foreign Office.

387
00:34:34.280 --> 00:34:38.512
make sure that it was you two
who delivered the Eye. Turn around.

388
00:34:38.600 --> 00:34:42.434
The Eye contains the elixir
from the Pool of Eternal Life.

389
00:34:44.440 --> 00:34:47.113
I need you to open it. Mrs O'Connell.

390
00:34:48.320 --> 00:34:49.469
No.

391
00:34:50.200 --> 00:34:52.430
You're going to use it to wake the Emperor.
aren't you?

392
00:34:52.520 --> 00:34:56.513
And his Terracotta Army.
At least. that's the general idea.

393
00:34:56.600 --> 00:34:59.990
Raising an army of mummies is insane.
Listen. Yang...

394
00:35:03.560 --> 00:35:05.232
Easy! Go easy.

395
00:35:06.040 --> 00:35:09.032
Time to open the sarcophagus. Move!

396
00:35:13.400 --> 00:35:16.597
Read the inscription! Now!

397
00:35:24.360 --> 00:35:26.954
Ancient Chinese isn't my forte.

398
00:35:27.040 --> 00:35:30.430
Here's some encouragement. Wilson!

399
00:35:31.560 --> 00:35:32.549
I'll do it!

400
00:35:32.640 --> 00:35:36.189
No. Evy. don't do it!
They're just gonna kill me. anyway.

401
00:35:40.040 --> 00:35:42.679
The inscription says
that only a drop of blood

402
00:35:42.760 --> 00:35:45.832
from a person of pure heart
can open the Eye.

403
00:35:47.800 --> 00:35:49.711
Your husband was right.

404
00:35:51.480 --> 00:35:52.959
No!

405
00:35:59.480 --> 00:36:03.837
Only the pure of heart would sacrifice
themselves for the one they love.

406
00:36:05.120 --> 00:36:06.599
Open it.

407
00:36:11.360 --> 00:36:14.158
You never called after our last date.

408
00:36:14.240 --> 00:36:16.470
I don't have time for games. Alex.

409
00:36:16.560 --> 00:36:19.791
You know my name. but I don't know yours.

410
00:36:19.880 --> 00:36:21.029
It's Lin.

411
00:36:21.120 --> 00:36:24.510
You want to explain to me
why you tried to kill me?

412
00:36:24.600 --> 00:36:25.669
We could do that.

413
00:36:25.760 --> 00:36:27.478
Or we could save your parents.

414
00:36:32.280 --> 00:36:34.840
Wilson. you son of a bitch!

415
00:37:25.000 --> 00:37:28.231
- Get on with it. O'Connell.
- All right.

416
00:37:46.440 --> 00:37:51.753
Once this touches him.
the Emperor will rise to rule again.

417
00:37:52.800 --> 00:37:53.789
Finish him off.

418
00:38:31.760 --> 00:38:34.035
Alex. please! Don't. That's...

419
00:38:34.600 --> 00:38:36.750
Don't. don't. Don't. please.

420
00:38:36.840 --> 00:38:39.400
No. don't. Alex. it's me. Please.

421
00:38:39.840 --> 00:38:43.435
It's not him. This is a eunuch! It's a decoy!

422
00:38:45.360 --> 00:38:47.316
Where the hell's the Emperor?

423
00:39:12.560 --> 00:39:13.754
Stay!

424
00:39:31.840 --> 00:39:33.432
Here we go again.

425
00:39:45.240 --> 00:39:47.037
I live to serve you. my Lord.

426
00:39:47.120 --> 00:39:48.633
I can help you become immortal.

427
00:39:48.720 --> 00:39:51.439
If you are lying. you will burn.

428
00:40:07.360 --> 00:40:11.433
Wait! Wait! You wait for me!
I'm coming with you! Wait. wait...

429
00:40:36.280 --> 00:40:37.599
Watch out!

430
00:40:42.680 --> 00:40:46.434
We got to put this mummy down fast!
The longer we wait. the stronger they get!

431
00:40:46.520 --> 00:40:48.750
Open the gate! Open the gate!

432
00:40:55.800 --> 00:40:59.475
Yeah. yeah. yeah. I know. Sorry. pal.
There's a mummy on the loose.

433
00:40:59.560 --> 00:41:00.788
- You wanna drive?
- Why not?

434
00:41:00.880 --> 00:41:02.598
God. I love a woman who can drive a truck.

435
00:41:02.680 --> 00:41:05.638
Hey. pal. I'm really sorry.
but you know what? Happy New Year!

436
00:41:05.960 --> 00:41:07.188
Hit it. honey!

437
00:41:12.320 --> 00:41:13.958
No! Move over!

438
00:41:15.200 --> 00:41:16.792
What? No!

439
00:41:16.880 --> 00:41:18.154
No!

440
00:41:24.960 --> 00:41:26.234
No!

441
00:41:27.720 --> 00:41:30.154
- What?
- Jonathan. get in the back!

442
00:41:31.440 --> 00:41:32.509
Sorry about the Rolls!

443
00:41:32.600 --> 00:41:34.909
You guys are like mummy magnets!

444
00:41:36.520 --> 00:41:38.988
- We have to turn you around!
- Okay.

445
00:41:44.640 --> 00:41:45.993
Excuse me.

446
00:41:48.360 --> 00:41:50.954
- Hey. we could use this!
- Give me that!

447
00:41:53.200 --> 00:41:56.476
- Oh. yeah. that's a better idea.
- Size counts!

448
00:41:56.560 --> 00:41:59.358
Stop mucking about! They're getting away!

449
00:42:00.240 --> 00:42:01.912
Just drive!

450
00:42:02.560 --> 00:42:04.676
Aim for the Emperor!
- Aim for the Emperor?

451
00:42:04.760 --> 00:42:07.320
- Light it up. Jonathan!
- I'm trying!

452
00:42:07.400 --> 00:42:08.469
Fire!

453
00:42:28.280 --> 00:42:29.713
Did we get him?

454
00:42:29.800 --> 00:42:31.836
- Fire!
- What. again?

455
00:42:31.920 --> 00:42:33.751
- Your ass is on fire!
- My ass?

456
00:42:33.840 --> 00:42:35.637
- Hold still!
- Rick. my ass is on fire!

457
00:42:35.720 --> 00:42:37.119
- Well. spank my...
- I'm putting it out!

458
00:42:37.200 --> 00:42:38.872
- Put me out. Rick!
- Just hold still!

459
00:42:38.960 --> 00:42:41.155
Spank my ass! Spank my ass!

460
00:42:41.240 --> 00:42:43.117
All right. here I come!

461
00:42:45.960 --> 00:42:47.678
Give me your hand!

462
00:42:53.640 --> 00:42:54.629
Come on!

463
00:42:55.200 --> 00:42:56.553
Watch out!

464
00:42:57.440 --> 00:42:58.509
Evy. where are you going?

465
00:42:58.600 --> 00:43:00.636
- Taking a short cut!
- Evy!

466
00:43:09.720 --> 00:43:11.676
- I told you it was a short cut!
- Right!

467
00:43:11.760 --> 00:43:13.557
Now he's chasing us!

468
00:43:17.880 --> 00:43:19.074
Hurry!

469
00:43:20.200 --> 00:43:22.760
Give me your hand.
Here. you're gonna need these.

470
00:43:22.840 --> 00:43:24.637
- Don't wait up for me.
- Where are you going?

471
00:43:24.720 --> 00:43:25.789
Out!

472
00:43:31.680 --> 00:43:34.240
- Where's Rick?
- Where do you think?

473
00:43:40.200 --> 00:43:41.519
Damn it!

474
00:43:45.480 --> 00:43:46.913
You're mine!

475
00:43:51.880 --> 00:43:55.350
- Give me your hand and get on this horse!
- Get back. Dad!

476
00:43:55.440 --> 00:44:00.195
Alexander Rupert O'Connell. you get
on the back of this horse this instant!

477
00:44:09.200 --> 00:44:13.193
Get out of the way! Get out of the way!
Oh. God!

478
00:44:20.160 --> 00:44:21.275
Evy!

479
00:44:22.320 --> 00:44:23.833
We've got to go back and help Rick!

480
00:44:23.920 --> 00:44:26.673
Rick! Forget Rick!
Here they come!

481
00:44:34.880 --> 00:44:36.472
I'll go after the Emperor.

482
00:44:36.560 --> 00:44:39.199
Trust me. I've got a little more experience
with mummies.

483
00:44:39.280 --> 00:44:42.636
And I have the only weapon
that can kill him.

484
00:44:42.720 --> 00:44:45.029
Okay. I'll cover you. Let's go!

485
00:44:53.040 --> 00:44:54.155
Lin!

486
00:45:11.160 --> 00:45:13.754
- I thought you were dead!
- He missed.

487
00:45:39.640 --> 00:45:40.993
Look out!

488
00:46:25.360 --> 00:46:29.717
- Thanks. Rick. Could you get the cab?
- Does it look like I have a wallet?

489
00:46:47.960 --> 00:46:50.599
You know. I would have killed the Emperor
if you two hadn't blown my cover.

490
00:46:50.680 --> 00:46:51.874
I had everything under control.

491
00:46:51.960 --> 00:46:54.110
Oh. yeah. that's exactly
what we were thinking.

492
00:46:54.200 --> 00:46:55.952
Yeah. well. good going.
you raised another mummy.

493
00:46:56.040 --> 00:46:57.917
And this bugger's got superpowers.

494
00:46:58.000 --> 00:47:01.117
He's got control over fire. water.
metal and who knows what else.

495
00:47:01.200 --> 00:47:02.235
And you dug him up anyway.

496
00:47:02.320 --> 00:47:03.992
Yeah. well. you're not gonna
pin this one on me. okay. Dad?

497
00:47:04.080 --> 00:47:06.230
- Am I?
- Oh. stop it. you two.

498
00:47:06.320 --> 00:47:09.596
No one's to blame here.
Wilson manipulated all of us.

499
00:47:09.680 --> 00:47:10.749
Yeah. that's true.

500
00:47:10.840 --> 00:47:12.831
I apologise for my parents.

501
00:47:12.920 --> 00:47:15.639
But I thought we worked
really well together.

502
00:47:16.120 --> 00:47:17.792
Except we failed.

503
00:47:19.920 --> 00:47:23.071
I'm sorry.
we haven't been properly introduced.

504
00:47:23.160 --> 00:47:25.628
- Who are you exactly?
- My name is Lin.

505
00:47:25.720 --> 00:47:28.951
My family has watched
over the Emperor's tomb for centuries.

506
00:47:29.040 --> 00:47:33.192
The Emperor cannot be killed unless
he is stabbed through the heart with this.

507
00:47:33.280 --> 00:47:35.874
My mother put a curse on it long ago.

508
00:47:37.200 --> 00:47:38.189
Mmm-hmm.

509
00:47:39.120 --> 00:47:41.634
Well. a quick family meeting. Alex.

510
00:47:43.320 --> 00:47:44.799
- Sit.
- Down.

511
00:47:46.760 --> 00:47:48.671
What do you really know about this girl?

512
00:47:48.760 --> 00:47:53.311
Well. not much. but after her help tonight.
I'm willing to go on a little faith.

513
00:47:53.400 --> 00:47:55.197
- Faith.
- Time is running out.

514
00:47:55.280 --> 00:47:57.669
You don't really believe in the concept
of personal space. do you?

515
00:47:57.760 --> 00:48:01.116
If the Emperor reaches Shangri-La
and drinks from the Pool of Eternal Life.

516
00:48:01.200 --> 00:48:03.953
he will raise his army
and no one will be safe.

517
00:48:04.040 --> 00:48:06.474
Much as I'd like to stay
this boyishly handsome forever.

518
00:48:06.560 --> 00:48:07.959
Shangri-La is a crock.

519
00:48:08.040 --> 00:48:09.917
Yeah. but that's what you used to say
about mummies. too. Jon.

520
00:48:10.000 --> 00:48:12.036
- You did pretty well off it.
- Good point.

521
00:48:12.120 --> 00:48:16.352
The Gateway to Shangri-La lies in
a mountain pass high in the Himalayas.

522
00:48:16.440 --> 00:48:18.510
Beyond it is a golden tower.

523
00:48:18.600 --> 00:48:22.149
Once the diamond is placed at the top.
it will point the way to Shangri-La.

524
00:48:22.240 --> 00:48:24.196
Yang still has the diamond.

525
00:48:24.280 --> 00:48:27.158
and that's where
he and the Emperor will go.

526
00:48:27.680 --> 00:48:28.669
She's right.

527
00:48:28.760 --> 00:48:31.718
All the legends of the Eye
mention the Gateway.

528
00:48:31.800 --> 00:48:33.870
I like her. Alex. She knows what's what.

529
00:48:33.960 --> 00:48:39.239
Now. just say that we were to believe you.
could you guide us there?

530
00:48:39.320 --> 00:48:42.596
Yes. I have been there once.
I remember the way.

531
00:48:45.320 --> 00:48:47.675
Himalayas. We're going to need a plane.

532
00:48:47.760 --> 00:48:50.433
Well. I know just the Mad Dog for the job.

533
00:48:53.680 --> 00:48:56.478
Well. any self-respecting pilot
would land on the valley floor.

534
00:48:56.560 --> 00:48:58.232
but I don't have any self-respect.

535
00:48:58.320 --> 00:49:00.470
so I'll put you down
halfway up the mountain.

536
00:49:00.560 --> 00:49:02.232
That should give us a good advantage.

537
00:49:02.320 --> 00:49:04.311
Of course.
I can't guarantee any of us will live.

538
00:49:04.400 --> 00:49:05.549
Great!

539
00:49:09.160 --> 00:49:12.869
I'd tell you to fasten your seatbelts.
but I was too cheap to buy any!

540
00:49:15.560 --> 00:49:17.835
- Why am I laughing?
- Here we go!

541
00:49:18.760 --> 00:49:21.877
Mad Dog. Mad Dog!
Ease up. ease up. ease up!

542
00:49:22.240 --> 00:49:23.639
Oh. God!

543
00:49:31.080 --> 00:49:32.752
Maguire!

544
00:49:34.360 --> 00:49:35.873
Come on. man!

545
00:49:36.320 --> 00:49:37.514
Mad Dog!

546
00:49:49.480 --> 00:49:51.072
Brake! No. no! Nobody move.

547
00:49:51.160 --> 00:49:53.799
Nobody move. nobody move!

548
00:50:06.680 --> 00:50:08.830
What is that God-awful smell?

549
00:50:10.120 --> 00:50:11.712
The yak yakked.

550
00:50:15.960 --> 00:50:18.190
Welcome to the modern world. my Lord.

551
00:50:18.720 --> 00:50:20.551
Why did you raise me?

552
00:50:20.960 --> 00:50:24.999
I love this land.
Only you can lead us back to greatness.

553
00:50:25.840 --> 00:50:28.115
What is in it for you?

554
00:50:29.640 --> 00:50:32.313
I want to serve as your general.

555
00:50:33.000 --> 00:50:35.355
The last general I trusted...

556
00:50:35.640 --> 00:50:38.313
betrayed me.

557
00:50:38.880 --> 00:50:41.519
I will not make that mistake.

558
00:50:47.680 --> 00:50:52.037
I cannot escape this curse
until I am immortal...

559
00:50:52.800 --> 00:50:54.233
General.

560
00:50:55.880 --> 00:50:57.791
I understand. my Lord.

561
00:50:58.080 --> 00:51:01.789
We need to find the Pool of Eternal Life.

562
00:51:02.640 --> 00:51:06.349
This will point the way.

563
00:51:26.920 --> 00:51:28.592
<i>Can't you see it's Mr McGuire</i>

564
00:51:28.680 --> 00:51:30.432
<i>come to court your sister Kate</i>

565
00:51:30.520 --> 00:51:34.433
<i>You know very well he owns the farm
a wee bit out...</i>

566
00:51:46.280 --> 00:51:49.317
<i>Delta-Tango-Alpha
to Ricochet. Come in. Ricochet.</i>

567
00:51:51.240 --> 00:51:53.629
Delta-Tango-Alpha. this is Ricochet.
Go ahead. Mad Dog.

568
00:51:53.720 --> 00:51:56.075
Yeah. you know that Yang fellow
you told me to keep me eye out for?

569
00:51:56.160 --> 00:51:57.309
<i>He's just shown up.</i>

570
00:51:57.400 --> 00:51:59.550
Ricochet out. Thanks. Mad Dog.

571
00:51:59.640 --> 00:52:01.232
That's us. people! Let's go!

572
00:52:01.320 --> 00:52:03.072
- Jonathan. wake up!
- What...

573
00:52:12.440 --> 00:52:13.953
Hold the line!

574
00:52:17.320 --> 00:52:18.435
Good. we're a little more than halfway.

575
00:52:18.520 --> 00:52:21.910
We're gonna...
We're gonna camp up there for the night.

576
00:52:34.160 --> 00:52:38.233
Lin says if we leave at first light.
we'll reach the Gateway by noon.

577
00:52:39.720 --> 00:52:43.508
Did she happen to mention how she knows
so much about the Gateway?

578
00:52:43.600 --> 00:52:46.273
No. not really. Kind of mysterious.

579
00:52:47.040 --> 00:52:49.679
She's certainly managed to enchant you.

580
00:52:51.760 --> 00:52:54.320
Come on. Alex. You obviously like her.

581
00:52:56.160 --> 00:52:59.630
Mom. the thin mountain air.
clearly messing with your head.

582
00:53:01.440 --> 00:53:03.556
Whatever secret she's hiding.

583
00:53:04.760 --> 00:53:06.796
I just don't want to see you get hurt.

584
00:53:06.880 --> 00:53:10.190
I appreciate that. but. you know.

585
00:53:10.280 --> 00:53:14.159
I've had my fair share of experience
with the opposite sex.

586
00:53:14.240 --> 00:53:15.355
Really?

587
00:53:17.040 --> 00:53:19.713
How many experiences
are we talking about?

588
00:53:20.960 --> 00:53:25.954
Well. you shouldn't ask questions you don't
want to know the answer to. okay. Mom?

589
00:53:26.040 --> 00:53:27.109
Right.

590
00:53:28.200 --> 00:53:29.997
Hey. Mom.

591
00:53:31.920 --> 00:53:35.390
I'm sorry I blamed you guys
for raising the Emperor.

592
00:53:46.120 --> 00:53:47.712
What's so funny?

593
00:53:50.800 --> 00:53:54.998
My mother is under the impression
there's something between us.

594
00:53:55.080 --> 00:53:56.991
I hope nothing romantic.

595
00:53:59.880 --> 00:54:03.316
Yeah. well. I told her there
was no chance of that.

596
00:54:03.400 --> 00:54:05.675
We're complete opposites.
you and me. right?

597
00:54:05.760 --> 00:54:10.595
You guard tombs. I raid them.
You like ancient knives. I'm into guns.

598
00:54:11.280 --> 00:54:13.635
Those are some
pretty insurmountable odds.

599
00:54:13.720 --> 00:54:15.870
- Absolutely.
- Well. good.

600
00:54:16.720 --> 00:54:20.759
Now that we've cleared that up.
we can focus on taking down the Emperor.

601
00:54:20.840 --> 00:54:22.398
I agree totally.

602
00:54:24.920 --> 00:54:27.514
Besides. you're not my type.

603
00:54:30.360 --> 00:54:34.319
Of course not. You don't like a woman
who can knock you on your backside.

604
00:54:36.520 --> 00:54:38.829
The expression is "kick my ass."

605
00:54:39.800 --> 00:54:42.189
And for the record. you didn't.

606
00:54:44.800 --> 00:54:47.917
Yeah. it's not easy being me. you know.

607
00:54:48.000 --> 00:54:49.638
Then again. I don't suppose
it's easy being you.

608
00:54:49.720 --> 00:54:51.790
is it. Geraldine. old girl?

609
00:54:51.880 --> 00:54:53.996
If I'd met a girl like you. Geraldine...

610
00:54:54.080 --> 00:54:56.878
You know. hard-working.
you don't say much.

611
00:54:57.880 --> 00:55:01.156
you're a little bit hairy. but I don't mind that.

612
00:55:11.800 --> 00:55:13.950
There it is! We found it!

613
00:55:21.600 --> 00:55:23.556
The Gateway of Shangri-La!

614
00:55:30.760 --> 00:55:34.548
Go. girl! Go! You're free!

615
00:55:34.640 --> 00:55:37.712
Go. Geraldine! Live free!

616
00:55:47.480 --> 00:55:50.074
What did you do now? Rob an armoury?

617
00:55:51.200 --> 00:55:53.475
Have you ever seen a Walther P38?

618
00:55:53.560 --> 00:55:55.710
Looks pretty anaemic
compared to the Peacekeeper.

619
00:55:55.800 --> 00:55:59.031
Well. it's not about size. Dad.
It's about stamina.

620
00:56:01.440 --> 00:56:02.919
You want power?

621
00:56:04.240 --> 00:56:09.155
I give you the Thompson submachine gun.
Fifty rounds a drum.

622
00:56:09.240 --> 00:56:12.277
- Twenty-five a mag.
- Tommy's good. Dad.

623
00:56:12.360 --> 00:56:13.998
but the cocking mechanism always jams.

624
00:56:14.080 --> 00:56:18.278
Here. Check out the Russian PPS
Personal Assault Weapon.

625
00:56:18.360 --> 00:56:19.998
Now. this is the future right here.

626
00:56:20.080 --> 00:56:23.311
You know. it's experience that wins the day.
It's not all about firepower.

627
00:56:23.400 --> 00:56:25.277
Boys! If I may...

628
00:56:25.360 --> 00:56:27.157
Do we have a plan for the Emperor?

629
00:56:27.240 --> 00:56:29.117
Yeah. We're gonna hit him
high. hard and fast

630
00:56:29.200 --> 00:56:30.872
and smash him like a Ming vase.

631
00:56:30.960 --> 00:56:33.952
- And if that doesn't work?
- We go to plan B.

632
00:56:34.040 --> 00:56:37.077
Plan B! You go upstairs.
you blow up that gold tower thing.

633
00:56:37.160 --> 00:56:39.196
- You light it up. We blow the guy sky high!
- Me?

634
00:56:39.280 --> 00:56:40.269
- You! What?
- Dad?

635
00:56:40.360 --> 00:56:42.396
So if the explosion doesn't kill us.
the avalanche will.

636
00:56:42.480 --> 00:56:43.913
- You got a better idea?
- Yeah. I do.

637
00:56:44.000 --> 00:56:45.797
I say we ambush him
with long-range rifles and silencers.

638
00:56:45.880 --> 00:56:46.915
Long-range. that's a better idea.

639
00:56:47.000 --> 00:56:48.035
Yeah. we can get in close. Dad.

640
00:56:48.120 --> 00:56:49.189
- Much better idea.
- And then we can finish him off

641
00:56:49.280 --> 00:56:50.838
- with Lin's dagger.
- Look. I'm sorry.

642
00:56:50.920 --> 00:56:53.480
I just don't put much faith
in your girlfriend's magic dagger.

643
00:56:53.560 --> 00:56:55.676
- Okay. Dad. she is not my girlfriend.
- You say that now.

644
00:56:55.760 --> 00:56:57.751
- but I still don't trust her.
- Well. I do.

645
00:56:57.840 --> 00:57:00.434
- So you should trust my judgement. okay?
- Look. kid.

646
00:57:00.520 --> 00:57:02.112
I've put down more mummies
in my time than you.

647
00:57:02.200 --> 00:57:03.553
You put down one mummy. Dad.

648
00:57:03.640 --> 00:57:06.712
Yeah. Same mummy twice!

649
00:57:11.040 --> 00:57:13.679
Hand me the green wire.
will you. please?

650
00:57:14.680 --> 00:57:16.511
Are you sure you know what you are doing?

651
00:57:16.600 --> 00:57:18.670
Of course. I've done this a hundred times.

652
00:57:18.760 --> 00:57:22.196
If the Emperor places the Eye up there.
all will be lost.

653
00:57:35.480 --> 00:57:37.152
Clear a path to the Golden Tower.

654
00:57:37.680 --> 00:57:40.558
Prove yourself to me.

655
00:57:54.160 --> 00:57:55.878
Let's give a warm O'Connell welcome!

656
00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:01.115
Fire!

657
00:58:13.680 --> 00:58:14.908
Bazooka!

658
00:58:19.880 --> 00:58:21.199
Fall back!

659
00:58:30.200 --> 00:58:32.475
Alex! Follow me!

660
00:58:47.200 --> 00:58:48.872
We gotta take out those bazookas!

661
00:58:50.840 --> 00:58:51.989
Go!

662
00:58:59.720 --> 00:59:01.039
Fall back!

663
00:59:01.560 --> 00:59:03.551
Move! Move! Move! Move!

664
00:59:10.760 --> 00:59:13.115
Time to go to plan B! Blow up the tower!

665
00:59:13.200 --> 00:59:14.997
Hey. I'm actually a little bit concerned
about plan B!

666
00:59:15.080 --> 00:59:16.433
Couldn't we go straight to plan C?

667
00:59:16.520 --> 00:59:19.034
Just make it go bang! I'll cover you!

668
00:59:20.160 --> 00:59:21.388
Come on.

669
00:59:22.200 --> 00:59:24.350
All right. let's go. go. go!
Come on. come on!

670
00:59:24.440 --> 00:59:26.192
Come on. Oh. be good.

671
00:59:45.200 --> 00:59:46.679
Set up a crossfire!

672
00:59:47.320 --> 00:59:48.514
Move it!

673
00:59:56.656 --> 00:59:58.294
My last round!

674
01:00:21.016 --> 01:00:25.009
- Abominable snowmen?
- The Tibetans call them yeti!

675
01:00:28.976 --> 01:00:30.329
Please! I need your help!

676
01:00:30.576 --> 01:00:32.532
These soldiers are evil!

677
01:00:34.616 --> 01:00:36.288
She speaks Yeti?

678
01:00:52.216 --> 01:00:53.808
Shoot! Kill them!

679
01:01:01.336 --> 01:01:04.009
Why do I always have to save the day?

680
01:01:04.616 --> 01:01:05.890
I hate it when the kid's right!

681
01:01:09.976 --> 01:01:11.568
Get the other guy!

682
01:01:12.496 --> 01:01:13.645
Thanks!

683
01:01:37.976 --> 01:01:39.204
Trouble!

684
01:02:17.136 --> 01:02:19.604
You can die slow or you can die fast.

685
01:02:40.776 --> 01:02:43.051
Yes! Yes! Yes!

686
01:02:44.336 --> 01:02:46.725
Yeah! I did it!

687
01:02:47.376 --> 01:02:51.528
Oh. Mother. I did it!
Time for a retreat. I think.

688
01:02:56.536 --> 01:03:01.326
I'm on your team! I'm a team player!
"One for all and all for me" kind of thing!

689
01:03:02.256 --> 01:03:05.646
The dynamite. all this dynamite!
We should get out of here!

690
01:03:20.816 --> 01:03:22.249
Back off! Back off!

691
01:03:22.576 --> 01:03:24.089
Run!

692
01:03:50.736 --> 01:03:54.206
I hate mummies!
They never play fair!

693
01:04:01.936 --> 01:04:04.211
Dad! Dad. what are you doing?

694
01:04:11.576 --> 01:04:15.012
Over here! Over here! Come on! Over here!

695
01:04:15.776 --> 01:04:17.095
Oh. no!

696
01:04:22.496 --> 01:04:23.531
Rick!

697
01:04:50.816 --> 01:04:52.693
Shangri-La.

698
01:05:01.056 --> 01:05:02.694
That's a diamond.

699
01:05:05.096 --> 01:05:06.575
I could use a diamond like that.

700
01:05:28.376 --> 01:05:29.604
Dad!

701
01:05:36.256 --> 01:05:38.690
Okay. hold it. Hold on there. Dad.

702
01:05:38.776 --> 01:05:41.768
All right. please. please. please
put pressure on it. okay. Dad?

703
01:05:41.856 --> 01:05:45.053
It's all right. it's all right.
We've been in tougher scrapes than this.

704
01:05:51.336 --> 01:05:52.894
Avalanche!

705
01:06:24.136 --> 01:06:26.206
- Help! Help me!
- Lin!

706
01:06:31.096 --> 01:06:32.529
Please! Help me!

707
01:07:12.536 --> 01:07:13.855
Yes!

708
01:07:15.136 --> 01:07:17.570
I've got it! And I'm still alive!

709
01:07:21.296 --> 01:07:23.730
Help me. please.
Somebody help me!

710
01:07:24.456 --> 01:07:27.175
- We're over here! Over here!
- Alex?

711
01:07:27.256 --> 01:07:29.724
- Mom. Mom. we're down here!
- Alex?

712
01:07:30.056 --> 01:07:31.455
We're over here!

713
01:07:43.336 --> 01:07:44.564
Oh. God.

714
01:07:45.936 --> 01:07:49.645
We've got to take him to Shangri-La now!
It's our only chance.

715
01:08:08.416 --> 01:08:09.735
We made it!

716
01:08:26.896 --> 01:08:28.249
The Pool.

717
01:08:38.896 --> 01:08:40.011
Mother.

718
01:08:41.456 --> 01:08:42.445
My sweet daughter.

719
01:08:50.976 --> 01:08:52.011
I beg you...

720
01:08:53.696 --> 01:08:55.493
My father is dying.

721
01:08:55.936 --> 01:08:57.164
They are my friends.

722
01:08:58.136 --> 01:08:59.455
Oh. please.

723
01:09:34.296 --> 01:09:35.615
Thank you.

724
01:09:36.976 --> 01:09:39.888
He must rest. We'll take him to my chamber.

725
01:09:57.136 --> 01:10:00.526
Where are you going. General?
Our destiny awaits.

726
01:10:05.496 --> 01:10:10.012
Well. it's not everyone that gets
their brother-in-law back from the dead.

727
01:10:10.616 --> 01:10:13.813
Yeah. give me my four score years
and ten any day.

728
01:10:18.616 --> 01:10:20.413
Is this Shangri-La?

729
01:10:29.976 --> 01:10:32.695
I could live here. Lots of opportunity.

730
01:10:34.616 --> 01:10:36.015
A casino.

731
01:10:40.736 --> 01:10:43.933
I was wrong to involve you in my revenge.

732
01:10:44.456 --> 01:10:45.889
No. mother.

733
01:10:46.936 --> 01:10:49.006
I would do anything for you.

734
01:10:57.936 --> 01:11:00.211
He's resting well. Thank you.

735
01:11:01.896 --> 01:11:04.205
How'd you get involved in all this?

736
01:11:04.296 --> 01:11:09.131
The Emperor murdered the only man
I ever loved. Lin's father.

737
01:11:10.576 --> 01:11:13.295
I would have died. too. by his hand.

738
01:11:13.376 --> 01:11:17.130
if the yeti had not found me
and brought me to this pool.

739
01:11:17.216 --> 01:11:20.174
Hang on a second.
How did this all happen?

740
01:11:20.256 --> 01:11:22.133
This was before Christ.

741
01:11:24.976 --> 01:11:27.649
How long were you guarding his tomb?

742
01:11:27.736 --> 01:11:29.328
Over 2.000 years.

743
01:11:35.256 --> 01:11:37.451
The Emperor must never be
allowed to reach the Pool.

744
01:11:37.536 --> 01:11:40.334
or he will have the power to raise his army.

745
01:11:40.416 --> 01:11:41.974
And once he becomes immortal.

746
01:11:42.056 --> 01:11:45.935
he can transform himself into
the most hideous creatures ever seen.

747
01:11:46.016 --> 01:11:48.849
I will take the first watch at the entrance.

748
01:11:55.296 --> 01:11:58.686
You know. I have no problem
dating an older woman.

749
01:12:01.456 --> 01:12:03.686
I'm afraid we can't be together.

750
01:12:04.576 --> 01:12:07.044
Wait. What? Why?

751
01:12:08.696 --> 01:12:11.130
Because I'm going to live forever.

752
01:12:11.856 --> 01:12:14.086
I don't want to watch you die.

753
01:12:14.976 --> 01:12:16.773
So what? That's it?

754
01:12:17.696 --> 01:12:20.608
You're just gonna sit
on the sidelines for eternity?

755
01:12:20.696 --> 01:12:23.654
My mother has mourned
my father for centuries.

756
01:12:24.216 --> 01:12:26.810
I don't know if my heart can bear it.

757
01:12:31.296 --> 01:12:34.333
People can live an entire lifetime
in one look.

758
01:12:36.456 --> 01:12:38.845
I watch my parents do it every day.

759
01:12:41.816 --> 01:12:42.726
Alex?

760
01:12:44.256 --> 01:12:46.724
Your father's awake. Get up here!

761
01:12:59.056 --> 01:13:00.250
Hello.

762
01:13:03.016 --> 01:13:06.053
If this is heaven. it looks pretty good so far.

763
01:13:13.936 --> 01:13:16.404
Nice to see some things never change.

764
01:13:33.776 --> 01:13:36.165
Go easy on him. He feels terrible.

765
01:13:41.616 --> 01:13:44.005
When I saw you lying there. Dad...

766
01:13:44.336 --> 01:13:47.089
I've never been so scared in my life.

767
01:13:48.616 --> 01:13:50.766
Well. that makes two of us.

768
01:13:51.776 --> 01:13:54.609
I mean. you know.
you're not supposed to die. you know?

769
01:13:54.696 --> 01:13:56.652
You're Ricochet O'Connell. right?

770
01:13:56.736 --> 01:13:59.853
You get beat up. you get tossed around.

771
01:13:59.936 --> 01:14:02.450
but. well. you're always standing there
in the end.

772
01:14:02.536 --> 01:14:05.608
I never really thought of
the world without you.

773
01:14:09.136 --> 01:14:10.535
Alex.

774
01:14:12.416 --> 01:14:14.088
the truth is.

775
01:14:16.456 --> 01:14:18.128
I'm just trying to...

776
01:14:20.136 --> 01:14:22.013
I'm just...

777
01:14:22.096 --> 01:14:23.245
I'm trying to be a good husband.

778
01:14:23.336 --> 01:14:24.655
I'm trying to be a good parent.

779
01:14:24.736 --> 01:14:28.172
And the truth is.
I've been dropping the ball lately. and...

780
01:14:28.256 --> 01:14:31.089
No. you know. I haven't been
the world's greatest son. you know?

781
01:14:31.176 --> 01:14:35.055
No. no. that's 'cause you get it
from her side of the family.

782
01:14:35.136 --> 01:14:36.455
Come here.

783
01:14:39.976 --> 01:14:41.250
My boys.

784
01:14:45.656 --> 01:14:48.375
You look tired. you should rest.

785
01:14:49.336 --> 01:14:50.451
I'll stay.

786
01:14:51.576 --> 01:14:53.646
Fate is about to deal its final hand.

787
01:14:53.976 --> 01:14:56.126
If we are to defeat the Emperor...

788
01:14:56.456 --> 01:14:59.926
I must ask for one more sacrifice.

789
01:15:00.336 --> 01:15:01.530
Anything. mother.

790
01:15:03.376 --> 01:15:05.367
Your immortality.

791
01:15:16.856 --> 01:15:19.370
Oh. no! His powers have been fully restored!

792
01:15:19.456 --> 01:15:20.730
Time to go.

793
01:15:43.376 --> 01:15:45.651
General Ming's daughter.

794
01:15:46.456 --> 01:15:48.686
Your child will be mine.

795
01:15:57.136 --> 01:15:59.047
He is immortal.

796
01:16:26.576 --> 01:16:29.693
Hey! You three-headed shape-shifting
son of a bitch!

797
01:16:39.976 --> 01:16:40.965
Lin!

798
01:16:51.496 --> 01:16:52.690
Alex!

799
01:16:56.176 --> 01:16:57.211
Alex!

800
01:17:06.016 --> 01:17:08.132
He's taking her back to his tomb
to raise his army!

801
01:17:08.216 --> 01:17:11.208
- Is there a faster way down from here?
- The yeti. They'll help.

802
01:17:11.296 --> 01:17:13.287
But he's already in the air. It'll be too late!

803
01:17:13.376 --> 01:17:17.369
Mad Dog can outfly a three-headed lizard
any day of the week! Let's go.

804
01:17:22.536 --> 01:17:24.367
Portside! Nine o'clock!

805
01:17:31.296 --> 01:17:33.856
Rick? Should I quit drinking?

806
01:17:39.496 --> 01:17:40.485
<i>Jonathan to Rick.</i>

807
01:17:40.576 --> 01:17:42.487
<i>You'd better get a move on if
you're gonna beat him to the tomb!</i>

808
01:17:42.576 --> 01:17:45.170
Yeah. yeah. just get back here as fast
as you can with the reinforcements.

809
01:17:45.256 --> 01:17:46.928
No sightseeing!

810
01:17:49.376 --> 01:17:51.048
Here. Dad.

811
01:17:51.136 --> 01:17:52.125
- Is that for me?
- Yeah.

812
01:17:52.216 --> 01:17:53.331
Nice.

813
01:17:54.096 --> 01:17:57.930
The Terracotta Army is not indestructible
until it crosses the Great Wall.

814
01:17:58.016 --> 01:18:01.247
That's comforting. How exactly are we
supposed to fend them off?

815
01:18:01.336 --> 01:18:02.530
When the Emperor built the Wall.

816
01:18:02.616 --> 01:18:03.935
he buried his enemies underneath it

817
01:18:04.016 --> 01:18:06.325
and cursed their souls
to hold it up for eternity.

818
01:18:06.416 --> 01:18:11.126
Most of them were conquered soldiers.
I will call them to battle once again.

819
01:18:11.216 --> 01:18:16.495
Unlock an altar. raise an army.
That sounds like a plan. Let's go.

820
01:18:42.336 --> 01:18:43.451
Grab her.

821
01:18:44.136 --> 01:18:45.774
Guard her with your life.

822
01:18:48.736 --> 01:18:49.885
Alex?

823
01:18:52.096 --> 01:18:54.564
- Where'd he go?
- Where do you think?

824
01:19:11.616 --> 01:19:13.174
AWAKE!

825
01:20:45.456 --> 01:20:47.492
Today you awake to a world...

826
01:20:48.216 --> 01:20:50.491
in the grip of chaos and corruption.

827
01:20:50.576 --> 01:20:52.567
Open the gates of the past

828
01:20:52.656 --> 01:20:55.090
and free the souls
of the wrongfully damned.

829
01:20:55.776 --> 01:20:57.573
I will restore order...

830
01:20:58.256 --> 01:21:00.451
I will retake what is mine.

831
01:21:01.136 --> 01:21:03.650
I will crush any idea of freedom.

832
01:21:03.776 --> 01:21:06.768
In the name of the ancestors
and the righteous.

833
01:21:06.856 --> 01:21:10.087
I sacrifice my immortality
and that of my daughter

834
01:21:10.176 --> 01:21:11.973
so that you may rise this day!

835
01:21:12.096 --> 01:21:13.893
I will slaughter without mercy.

836
01:21:14.216 --> 01:21:16.605
I will conquer without compassion.

837
01:21:16.936 --> 01:21:19.166
I will now lead you past the Great Wall.

838
01:21:19.536 --> 01:21:22.972
Once you cross. you will be indestructible.

839
01:21:23.896 --> 01:21:28.845
Bring down the wrath of the oppressed
on this Emperor and all who follow him!

840
01:21:29.336 --> 01:21:31.372
I raised you for one purpose...

841
01:21:31.656 --> 01:21:34.295
to enforce my will on the entire world!

842
01:21:34.936 --> 01:21:36.335
Long live the Emperor!

843
01:21:38.816 --> 01:21:42.047
I call upon the hundreds and the thousands

844
01:21:42.136 --> 01:21:46.812
that you may rise up and seize this moment
to take your victory.

845
01:21:46.896 --> 01:21:50.525
to take your justice
and to take your revenge!

846
01:22:08.776 --> 01:22:10.255
Zi Yuan.

847
01:22:16.376 --> 01:22:17.889
It's General Ming!

848
01:22:18.336 --> 01:22:19.894
Follow General Ming!

849
01:22:24.016 --> 01:22:27.008
Prepare for battle!

850
01:22:35.896 --> 01:22:38.694
These are...
They're good undead guys. right?

851
01:22:39.256 --> 01:22:42.168
Oh. no. no. no!

852
01:22:42.256 --> 01:22:44.451
Zi Yuan! Zi Yuan! Zi Yuan sent us!

853
01:22:44.536 --> 01:22:48.609
- Darling. I don't think he speaks English.
- We're with Zi Yuan!

854
01:22:48.696 --> 01:22:49.924
Zi Yuan?

855
01:22:50.456 --> 01:22:51.650
Right.

856
01:22:53.256 --> 01:22:54.484
Let's go.

857
01:22:55.456 --> 01:22:56.730
To battle!

858
01:23:16.456 --> 01:23:20.415
Freedom! Freedom! Freedom!

859
01:23:23.136 --> 01:23:24.649
Archers form up!

860
01:23:28.696 --> 01:23:29.924
Incoming!

861
01:23:42.656 --> 01:23:46.615
- Hey! That's my favourite blue shirt.
- I've always hated that shirt.

862
01:24:02.216 --> 01:24:03.774
Death to General Ming!

863
01:24:07.616 --> 01:24:08.935
Charge!

864
01:24:18.736 --> 01:24:20.772
Welcome to the 20th century!

865
01:24:36.936 --> 01:24:39.291
We can't let them cross the wall!

866
01:26:02.456 --> 01:26:03.809
You are no longer immortal.

867
01:26:43.136 --> 01:26:45.775
Honey! Fall back to higher ground!

868
01:26:52.176 --> 01:26:54.406
I really hate mummies!

869
01:26:54.496 --> 01:26:56.726
It seems the feeling's mutual!

870
01:27:00.336 --> 01:27:02.372
Shut up. clay boy! Fore!

871
01:27:02.976 --> 01:27:04.091
Run!

872
01:27:16.496 --> 01:27:18.009
- Catch!
- Got it!

873
01:27:19.976 --> 01:27:24.174
Next time I say. "We've been in tougher
scrapes than this." I mean this!

874
01:27:48.776 --> 01:27:51.973
Die. you mummy bastards! Die!

875
01:27:52.056 --> 01:27:54.968
There is no call for bad language!

876
01:27:57.136 --> 01:28:00.253
Jonathan certainly knows
how to make an entrance!

877
01:28:25.776 --> 01:28:27.494
Any regrets. darling?

878
01:28:29.536 --> 01:28:31.413
None. Not ever.

879
01:28:40.456 --> 01:28:43.254
- You okay?
- Yeah. sure. no problem.

880
01:28:43.336 --> 01:28:45.725
We had it completely under control.

881
01:28:48.456 --> 01:28:51.050
This guy ever run out of tricks?

882
01:28:55.256 --> 01:28:56.530
No!

883
01:29:03.456 --> 01:29:04.889
Mother! No!

884
01:29:07.616 --> 01:29:08.844
Mother!

885
01:29:13.576 --> 01:29:15.771
Mother! Mother!

886
01:29:25.656 --> 01:29:27.567
Pierce through his heart.

887
01:29:30.296 --> 01:29:34.608
You must live and fight on.

888
01:29:53.216 --> 01:29:55.684
She said through the heart.

889
01:29:55.776 --> 01:29:58.210
Through the heart. Let's go.

890
01:30:11.536 --> 01:30:12.571
Get in!

891
01:30:13.416 --> 01:30:16.010
The O'Connells are going to
stop the Emperor!

892
01:30:27.176 --> 01:30:29.485
So. Dad. what's the plan?

893
01:30:29.576 --> 01:30:31.009
Divide and conquer!

894
01:30:31.096 --> 01:30:34.054
No offence.
but isn't that a little short on detail?

895
01:30:34.736 --> 01:30:37.125
- Twelve o'clock low!
- Hang on!

896
01:30:45.056 --> 01:30:46.409
Remember our deal!

897
01:30:46.496 --> 01:30:49.010
When this is over.
my men get to drink for free!

898
01:30:49.096 --> 01:30:51.894
You can have the whole damn bar
for all I care!

899
01:30:51.976 --> 01:30:54.570
I'm getting the hell out of China.

900
01:31:25.096 --> 01:31:27.451
I dug you up...

901
01:31:28.336 --> 01:31:30.691
and I'm gonna put you down.

902
01:32:00.736 --> 01:32:03.375
Alex? Alex!

903
01:33:00.896 --> 01:33:01.931
Let go!

904
01:33:02.016 --> 01:33:03.051
Never!

905
01:33:06.816 --> 01:33:09.649
Enough tricks! Where's your honour?

906
01:33:12.656 --> 01:33:14.294
Fight like a man!

907
01:33:51.456 --> 01:33:53.048
Divide

908
01:33:54.576 --> 01:33:55.975
and conquer.

909
01:34:40.736 --> 01:34:43.455
Now you can rule in hell.

910
01:35:08.736 --> 01:35:10.408
The Emperor is dead.

911
01:35:10.696 --> 01:35:12.288
The Emperor is dead!

912
01:35:57.296 --> 01:36:01.255
- Evening. girls. You're looking well.
- Good evening. Mr Maguire.

913
01:36:02.096 --> 01:36:05.725
- It's a fine night to be me.
- You dance great for an old lady.

914
01:36:06.256 --> 01:36:08.690
Someone told me to stop living
on the sidelines.

915
01:36:08.776 --> 01:36:11.688
- Well. he sounds like a smart guy.
- He is.

916
01:36:23.216 --> 01:36:26.572
So I guess Dash and Scarlet
have their next adventure?

917
01:36:26.656 --> 01:36:29.409
Why write about it when you can live it?

918
01:36:30.496 --> 01:36:34.535
There's something incredibly romantic
about vanquishing the undead.

919
01:36:35.336 --> 01:36:37.804
Even more romantic doing it with you.

920
01:36:38.576 --> 01:36:41.295
- Kiss me.
- Don't have to ask me twice.

921
01:36:50.056 --> 01:36:51.648
- Can I get your bag. sir?
- No. no. no.

922
01:36:51.736 --> 01:36:53.647
Don't touch it. don't touch it.

923
01:36:53.736 --> 01:36:54.725
Where are you off to. Mr Carnahan?

924
01:36:54.816 --> 01:36:57.091
Someplace where they don't have mummies.

925
01:36:57.176 --> 01:36:59.895
- Step on it! I've got a plane to catch.
- Yes. sir.

926
01:36:59.976 --> 01:37:03.491
<i>Yeah. Ciao. ciao. Shanghai.</i>

927
01:37:03.576 --> 01:37:05.007
Peru.
here I come.

928
01:37:08.536 --> 01:37:12.814
Soon after. mummies were found in Peru.

929
01:46:57.856 --> 01:46:58.845
Subtitles by LeapinLar

930
01:46:59.305 --> 01:47:59.625
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
